Finding: {"title":"Void/refund transaction lookups have no flightSchoolId scoping and no idempotency guard against double-void/double-refund","severity":"HIGH","area":"State machine / authorization","files":["src/server/routes/routes-micamp.ts"],"detail":"POST /micamp/payments/:id/void (L595-660) and /refund (L662-738) load the transaction purely by `eq(schema.paymentTransactions.id, txId)` with no flightSchoolId filter tied to the admin caller's own school — any admin (of any school, since requireAdmin() doesn't check org membership per the finding above) can void or refund any transaction across the entire platform by guessing/enumerating a transaction UUID. Additionally, the refund path has no accumulation check: a transaction can be refunded multiple times as long as each individual partialAmount < transaction.amount, since status is only flipped to 'refunded' when `partialAmount >= transaction.amount` (L703) but nothing sums prior refunds against the original amount — repeated partial refunds (e.g. refund $1 nine times) could exceed the original charge with no guard, and each is a live money-movement call to MiCamp.","impact":"Cross-tenant unauthorized void/refund of another school's revenue. Over-refund beyond the original transaction amount is possible via repeated small partial refunds, resulting in MiCamp being asked to refund more than was ever charged (real financial loss).","recommendation":"Scope the transaction lookup by the admin's own flightSchoolId. Before issuing a partial refund, sum all prior completed 'refund' rows referencing this transaction's id and reject if `sum(priorRefunds) + requestedAmount > transaction.amount`.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

